<PolicyPage title="Editorial Policy — Love Mallacoota" description="The publication and moderation rules for Love Mallacoota community information." canonicalPath="/editorial-policy.html" prefix="Editorial" accent="Policy" lede="Factual local information, open to everyone, checked before publication and corrected when needed.">
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>Events, notices, group updates, directory listings, school and sport information, local history and practical visitor information supplied by the people or organisations responsible for it.</p>
  <h2>What we do not publish</h2>
  <p>Personal attacks, political campaigning, unverified allegations about named people or businesses, discriminatory material, or contributions that place someone at unreasonable risk.</p>
  <h2>Sources and attribution</h2>
  <p>We identify the source organisation or person where useful, link to authoritative material, and distinguish sponsored material from editorial or community information.</p>
  <h2>Moderation</h2>
  <p>Submissions are reviewed for relevance, accuracy, safety and compliance with this policy. If we decline a genuine community submission, we aim to explain why.</p>
  <h2>Emergency information</h2>
  <p>We relay official information only and never present Love Mallacoota as an emergency authority. See the <a href="/emergency.html">emergency information page</a>.</p>
</PolicyPage>
